  m_Name: Book_DryingFood
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GrandmasHouse::GrandmasHouse.Data.NoteData
  kind: 3
  title: Drying Food
  recipe: {fileID: 0}
  body: 
  marginNote: 
  pages:
  - 'Drying food


    Lay produce on the tray and switch the dehydrator on. Half
    a day later it''s dried: shrunk, darker, and good for a month or more where fresh
    would rot in a week.


    Dried food goes straight into the soup pot, no chopping.
    The dehydrator runs on electricity.'
